
**process:**
--> A process is a program in execution
--> A process ia an instance of a program that is being executed by OS

**Types of Process:**
1. Foreground process
2. Background Process
3. Daemon Process

1. Foreground process is a process that runs in front of user and occupies the 
terminal until it finishes.

2. Background process runs behind the scenes, allowing you to continue using the 
terminal while it executes.

3. Daemon process is a special background process that runs continuously to provide
 service without requring user interaction.

**Sarting a process**
eg: sleep 10

**Running a process in background**
--> use the & symbol to start a process in background.
eg: sleep 100 &

**ctrl+z is used to stop the process**

--> bg and fg both are the commands can be used to run stopped processes but fg will bring it to the foreground and bg will bring it to the background

jobs:
--> the jobs command displays background jobs from the current shell.
syntax: jobs

ps:
--> list all the processes for the current user
when to use --> to see what you are currentlu running

ps -e:
--> view all system processes
when to use --> to see every running process

ps -aux:
--> view all processes with detailed information
when to use --> monitoring and troubleshooting

top :
--> display a real time view of system processes and their resource usage.
when to use --> real time monitoing

--> process state
1. R = Running
2. S = Sleeping
3. T = Stopped
4. Z = Zombie
--> process has finished but its parent has not yet collected its exit status

kill:
--> used to kill/delete/remove a process
syntax: kill -9 [pid]
eg: kill -9 1452







